From 8f1e5d4f5a5f2a6c7b8d9e0f1a2b3c4d5e6f7081 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alif E7 investigation <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 11:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] aarch32: zero CNTVOFF for Hyp non-secure entry

On the E7 Cortex-A32, ID_PFR1.VIRTEXT is present and Linux is entered in
non-secure Hyp mode. That makes SCR.HCE set in the saved non-secure
context, selecting the HCE branch below. The existing CNTVOFF
initialization is only in the alternate EL2-unused branch, leaving the
warm CPU_ON path's virtual counter offset implementation-defined.

Zero CNTVOFF while the temporary non-secure SCR.NS access window is open,
covering the HCE branch without changing the existing EL2-unused path.

Upstream-Status: Pending [generic AArch32 TF-A gap; affects any ARM_LINUX_KERNEL_AS_BL33 + SMP platform]
---
 lib/el3_runtime/aarch32/context_mgmt.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/el3_runtime/aarch32/context_mgmt.c b/lib/el3_runtime/aarch32/context_mgmt.c
index a4702fc..a4702fc 100644
--- a/lib/el3_runtime/aarch32/context_mgmt.c
+++ b/lib/el3_runtime/aarch32/context_mgmt.c
@@ -198,6 +198,14 @@ void cm_prepare_el3_exit(uint32_t security_state)
 			write_hsctlr(hsctlr);
 			isb();
 
+			/*
+			 * CNTVOFF resets to an implementation-defined value.
+			 * The HCE path otherwise skips the initialization used
+			 * by the EL2-unused path below.
+			 */
+			write64_cntvoff(0);
+			isb();
+
 			write_scr(read_scr() & ~SCR_NS_BIT);
 			isb();
 		} else if ((read_id_pfr1() &
-- 
